# Dungeon Finder any level (m7, owner 2026-11-26): upstream's LFG.AnyLevel + AiPlayerbot.LfgAnyLevel (write-confs), no code
# of ours. A level-90 character queues Deadmines (326, level 15-21) as a tank: stock rules reject it (too high level); with
# AnyLevel it queues, and random bots within +-3 levels (AiPlayerbot.LfgAnyLevel.LevelWindow) fill the group -> proposal (3)
# or in the dungeon (5). LFG states: 0 none, 1 role check, 2 queued, 3 proposal, 5 dungeon.
# Level 90: bot crowding (dynamic level brackets) gathers most bots in the test character's bracket, which is 90 for most of a run.

> .arpg test setup Arpgtest 90 elwynn-northshire
? ok .*\(online\)
~ 4000
> .botscenario Arpgtest lfgleave
? lfgleave
> .botscenario Arpgtest lfgjoin 326 2
? lfgjoin Arpgtest dungeon=326 .*ok state=
> .botscenario Arpgtest lfgstate
? lfgstate player=[1-5]\b
# Bots check the queue every 30 s and need a healer + 3 damage from the bots within +-3 levels: up to ~3 minutes.
# Polled every 2 s: the headless client never accepts the proposal, so it expires after ~40 s and drops the queue.
> .botscenario Arpgtest lfgstate
*300 lfgstate player=[35]\b
> .botscenario Arpgtest lfgleave
? lfgleave
